section.center(data-name="Start")
	h1 Smallcontrol
	h3 in a Simplemenu bar

section.center(data-name="Vertical")
	section.center
		h2 If you use Simplemenu...
		p ...and add .controls to it, the controls (the navigation arrows) move into the bar. Not just Smallcontrol. Normal controls too.
	section.center
		p The controls then get the colours as defined for the bar.
	section.center
		p And keep working as before.

section.center(data-name="Light" data-background-color="#fff")
	h2 On a light slide
	p That works too.

section(data-name="Setup")
	section
		h3 Setup
	section
		p.small If you put a #[code div] with the class #[code controls] in the bar, then Simplemenu moves Reveal’s controls into it. Smallcontrol does the rest.
		pre
			code.hljs.javascript(data-line-numbers).
				Reveal.initialize({
					simplemenu: {
						barhtml: {
							header: "&lt;nav class='menubar'&gt;"
								+ "&lt;div class='padbox'&gt;&lt;/div&gt;"
								+ "&lt;ul class='menu'&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;"
								+ "&lt;div class='padbox'&gt;"
								+ "&lt;div class='controls'&gt;&lt;/div&gt;"
								+ "&lt;/div&gt;"
								+ "&lt;/nav&gt;"
						}
					},
					plugins: [ Simplemenu, Smallcontrol ]
				});
	section.center
		h4 That’s it!
